Root cause:
The bug was caused by the inclusion of platform-specific code in the native compilation process that was not properly guarded for non-UNIX platforms, leading to compilation errors on Windows after changes made in HADOOP-7824. The initialization of Java constants specific to UNIX was being attempted on Windows, which does not support those constants.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
SET_INT_OR_RETURN(env, clazz, S_IXUSR);
```
Reason:
This line attempts to initialize a Java constant specific to UNIX (`S_IXUSR`), which is not defined on Windows. The lack of proper platform checks resulted in compilation errors when this code was executed on a non-UNIX platform after the changes made in HADOOP-7824.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef UNIX
SET_INT_OR_RETURN(env, clazz, S_IXUSR);
#endif
```
Reason:
By wrapping the initialization of the UNIX-specific constant in an `#ifdef UNIX` preprocessor directive, the code ensures that this line is only compiled and executed on UNIX platforms. This prevents the compilation errors on Windows, effectively fixing the bug.


